# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_iac_recall.py" "IAC RECALL GATE: PASS" "IaC cross-module reference recall (the opposite failure of the #330 per-dir precision fix) -- genuine cross-directory Terraform module-output contracts still couple" "iac-recall: a Terraform ROOT/ENV module that instantiates a CHILD via a LOCAL source and consumes its OUTPUT (module.X.out where module \"X\" { source = \"./child\" }) couples to the child file that DEFINES output \"out\" -- a real cross-directory contract with NO code edge that per-dir namespacing of type.name (#330) cannot see and previously dropped to silence; recall preserved across nested ../../ paths and when the output lives in the child's main.tf; PRECISION PRESERVED (#330): two unrelated child dirs each defining the SAME output name do NOT share a node, so a consumer of childA is never coupled to childB's identically-named output; a registry/remote module source (not ./ or ../) resolves to no local dir and couples NOTHING; never-crash on malformed HCL (unterminated block, missing source, absolute-path source, undeclared instance, binary bytes) -> no cross-module edges, never raises; plus direct unit checks of the source-resolution and reference-parse primitives; content-free (module-instance names + output names + resolved dir paths only, never resource values)." "IaC cross-module recall: the #330 multi-definer fix namespaced Terraform resource ids by the defining module DIRECTORY to kill the aws_iam_role.this same-name false coupling (measured 64 to 18 pairs on terraform-aws-eks). This gate audits the OPPOSITE failure that namespacing creates -- a GENUINE cross-directory contract dropped to silence. The canonical such contract is a root/env module that declares module \"X\" { source = \"./child\" } and references module.X.output: renaming the child's output \"name\" breaks the root, a real coupling carried by the module instance + its local source path (NOT a shared type.name), invisible to call/import graphs AND to the per-dir type.name namespacing. The fix resolves the consumer's own LOCAL source path to the child directory and couples it (queries edge) to the child file(s) that DEFINE the referenced output (alters edge) through a child-dir-namespaced output node, mirroring every sibling cross-substrate detector (_cg_schema migration to query). RECALL-SAFE and #330-PRESERVING: the coupling anchor is the consumer's explicitly-declared local source resolved to a real child dir, never a coincidental shared name -- two unrelated dirs that each define output \"id\" get DISTINCT nodes, so a consumer cannot be dragged into an unrelated same-name dir, and a remote/registry source resolves to no dir and couples nothing. Content-free (names + paths only). Never-crash (malformed HCL degrades to no edges). Gate 129." 9
